      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "i get the same issue, but it is very frequent. happens in almost any world, and at any time. happens more often if there is a group of more than 3 people nearby. the bug gets worse the longer i am online. restarting the game fixes it, but only for a few minutes until it starts again. ive been playing VRC for a fairly long time but it only recently began, and got MUCH worse with the two latest updates as of sept. 12 2020 - it is NOT as simple as \"reversed stereo\" it can be more accurately described as 'incorrect position and rotation of audio source'. it can make players sound closer, farther away, or in a different direction than they are. in a group of 6 or more people it becomes a completely unplayable mess of audiosensory overload as voices originate from seemingly random locations around your head.\ni have tried a variety of adjustments to audio devices, changing device completely, and completely reinstalling VRchat fresh. none of this had any impact.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
