      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64873f159cf028090ce2c2e2|full_name}: So the audio straight-up swapping ears isn't really a thing anymore, but positional audio DOES consistently break in larger worlds and has done so for YEARS.  It'll sound like player voices are coming right at your left or right ear, rather than position correctly from the intended speaker.  \n\nThis generally occurs about once a night for me if I'm hanging out in larger party worlds with music and people talking, and the best causes I've been able to determine are either a missing VRC audio source spatializer on a world's audio component breaks player audio somehow (I've had this happen in my own world without one, adding it has caused this to never happen since).  Any large club world will do this with a high player cap and an active video player (Smashed is one that's consistently done it to me, Drinking Night will too sometimes if it's highly-populated)\n\nThe other best guess I've had is it's a memory or caching issue of some kind that causes the audio engine to start struggling, because it tends to fail on a single person more often than not (ie; you hear one or two specific players sounding like they're right in your ear or in the wrong place) with other player's voices coming from their actual location.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
